Notes on DCM procedure in SPM
-----------------------------

Step 1: GLM design

[Basically the setup for FLA I was doing]

* New Batch: Stats > fMRI model specification
* Directory: select the GLM folder
* Units for design: Scans
* Interscan interval: our TR value in seconds
* Data & Design:
	> Scans: choose all functional scans
	> Conditions: using timing vectors, add these in
	
* Second module: Stats > model estimation
* Select SPM.mat, click on Dependency button + proposed item

Step 2: Adding contrasts

* New Batch: Stats > Contrast manager
* Select SPM.mat from previous step
* Contrast Sessions:
	> One F-contrast
	> Three t-contrasts (for each condition)
	
Step 3: Identifying ROIs based on contrasts

* View contrast in spm window
* Launch "contrast" option, then pair with second contrast
* Overlay > Previous Sections
* Navigate to coordinates of interest
* Select "eigenvariate" > label region accordingly

Step 4: Building the DCM with nodes

* Dynamic Causal Modeling button
* Specify > SPM.mat file associated to previous parts
* Give model a name
* Select VOIs in order
* Specify slice timing details (?)
* define the extrinsic connections between regions
